      {
        "id": 1842579597,
        "content": "### Describe the background or context\nI experimented today with the 'query' command after enabling in my fork always received \r\n`Invalid syntax for query command` error, see https://github.com/gitcoindev/ubiquibot/pull/3\r\nI was able to run this command only because I analysed the regex in https://github.com/ubiquity/ubiquibot/blob/development/src/handlers/comment/handlers/query.ts\r\nBy default GitHub adds an empty space after username after typing @username and this is rejected as the regex does not allow any white space after user name.\r\n### Describe the solution\nProposal to fix this: Update the regex to allow to add an optional empty white space after user name.",
