      {
        "id": 1292179383,
        "content": "`match` function behaves [differently](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/String/match#return_value) when a regex is global like yours `/g`. I think we don't need global regex because we are just searching for one instance of query",
        "url": "https://github.com/ubiquity/ubiquibot/pull/611#discussion_r1292179383",
        "commentType": "PULL_COLLABORATOR",
        "diffHunk": "@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ export const query = async (body: string) => {\n     return `Skipping '/query' because of no issue instance`;\n   }\n \n-  const regex = /^\\/query\\s@(\\w+)$/;\n+  const regex = /(?<=\\/query @)\\w+/g\n   const matches = body.match(regex);",
